e\": 0.3}, {\"category\": \"footprint_mismatch\", \"components\": [\"C3\"], \"pins\": [\"C3.1\", \"C3.2\"], \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(C3-Pad1)\"], \"observed\": \"C3 is a 0.1uF capacitor (Device:C) assigned an inductor footprint (L_0805), and both of its pins are left unconnected (pin 2 appears on no net).\", \"expected\": \"A capacitor should carry a capacitor footprint, and a part with no connections should not be placed on the board.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(value \\\"0.1uF\\\")\\n      (footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"}], \"impact\": \"The part has no electrical function. It is a stray or mis-assigned component that could be mistaken for a decoupling capacitor during assembly.\", \"confidence\": 0.2}], \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is the SKW92A LAN_PORT3_TX\u00b1 pins (U6.13/U6.14) being tied to GND, which is a clear electrical fault in the netlist. Lower-confidence observations are the 4.7 \u00b5F value of C1 against the reference 1 \u00b5F and a floating capacitor C3 carrying an inductor footprint.\"}",
